From: Abraham van der Merwe <abz@frogfoot.com>
Date: Sun, 26 Apr 2026 17:38:24 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 9/9] Item 21: cleanup, packaging, release prep for 1.1.0
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Drop all HAVE_GEOS_* feature-detection gates from config.m4, geos.c,
  arginfo.h. Every gate covered a 3.10-or-earlier symbol; the new floor
  is GEOS 3.11.0 (Q5.9 in implementation plan).
- config.m4: hard-fail at configure time when geos-config --version is
  below 3.11.0 (AS_VERSION_COMPARE).
- package.xml: bump release/api to 1.1.0; rewrite description and
  release notes to summarise the new surface.
- debian/changelog: prepend 1.1.0+git20260426-1~jammy1 entry covering
  items 2-20.
- README.md: rewrite for the extended fork — class/feature matrix,
  GEOS version requirement, build instructions, attribution.
- debian/patches: clear obsolete 0001-0006 PHP-version compat patches
  + use-zend_ce_exception-php8.5 (all integrated upstream in 1.1.0
  source). Empty quilt series.
- tests/TestHelper.php: track explicitly (was caught by tests/*.php
  blanket ignore, breaking make test from a fresh checkout).
- .gitignore: exempt tests/TestHelper.php; add debian build artefacts.
- upstream-patches/: git format-patch dfe1ab1..HEAD output (8 patches),
  basis of the Debian/Ubuntu contribution.

Final regression: 25/25 .phpt green against libgeos 3.14.1 / PHP 8.1.
Valgrind: only PHP module-init one-shot allocations remain
(zend_register_functions / zend_register_internal_class_ex), no
per-call leaks in geos.c userland paths.
.deb built clean: php-geos_1.1.0+git20260426-1~jammy1_amd64.deb.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
