+From 4649337cc64b71470b2f26cca66bed6cd33762b7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: Abraham van der Merwe <abz@frogfoot.com>
+Date: Sun, 26 Apr 2026 16:08:55 +0200
+Subject: [PATCH 2/8] tests: update fixtures for libgeos 3.14.1 default
+ behaviour
+
+GEOS 3.14.1 introduced several backwards-compatible default-behaviour
+changes that surface in our 1.0.0-era test fixtures. Updates each .phpt
+to expect the new defaults and outputs:
+
+- WKT writer: canonicalises -0 -> 0; default trim is now TRUE;
+  setRoundingPrecision(0) yields trimmed output; setOutputDimension
+  accepts 4 (XYZM); error message text broadened.
+- WKB writer/reader: getOutputDimension default is 4; accepts 4 as
+  valid input; error message broadened.
+- Geometry: empty intersection returns input-type EMPTY rather than
+  GEOMETRYCOLLECTION EMPTY for POINT-POINT and similar same-type cases;
+  polygon ring start vertex normalised to lex-smallest; collection
+  member ordering changed; mitre-join buffer corner clamping shifted;
+  offsetCurve right-side reverses orientation and densifies
+  interpolation; MULTIPOINT WKT format now 'MULTIPOINT ((x y), ...)';
+  argument-type exception messages broadened ('Polygon' -> 'Surface',
+  'LineString' -> 'Curve' / 'SimpleCurve' depending on context).
+- Three pre-existing WKT parse-typo testcases that GEOS 3.10's lenient
+  parser silently accepted: extra ')' in GEOMETRYCOLLECTION /
+  MULTIPOLYGON literals. Fixed.
+
+All 6 .phpt tests now pass against libgeos 3.14.1.
