+From 776397705293daca0d40c75bfbe80a4d71f71d01 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: Abraham van der Merwe <abz@frogfoot.com>
+Date: Sun, 26 Apr 2026 16:19:19 +0200
+Subject: [PATCH 3/8] Add GEOSCoordSeq class + Geometry sibling accessors
+MIME-Version: 1.0
+Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
+Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit
+
+Implements item 2 of docs/04-implementation-plan.md — the foundation
+class for coordinate-sequence access, required by curved geometries,
+factory constructors, and full Z/M support.
+
+GEOSCoordSeq class (new):
+  __construct(int $size, int $dim = 2, bool $hasM = false)
+  getSize(), getDimensions(), hasZ(), hasM(), isCCW()
+  setX/Y/Z/M($i, $v), getX/Y/Z/M($i)
+  setXY/setXYZ, getXY/getXYZ
+  copyFromArrays($x, $y, ?$z, ?$m)
+  copyToArrays() returning x/y/z/m arrays
+
+Lifecycle invariants documented inline in geos.c:
+  1. PHP-owned: dtor calls GEOSCoordSeq_destroy_r.
+  2. Ownership transfers to a geometry on createPoint/etc handoff
+     (set relay to NULL after handoff to avoid double-free).
+  3. GEOSGeom_getCoordSeq_r returns non-owning; clone before
+     wrapping in a PHP object.
+
+Sibling additions on GEOSGeometry:
+  hasM() : bool                     wraps GEOSHasM_r
+  getZ() : float                    wraps GEOSGeomGetZ_r
+  getM() : float                    wraps GEOSGeomGetM_r
+  getCoordSeq() : GEOSCoordSeq      type-checks for
+                                    Point/LineString/LinearRing,
+                                    clones the underlying seq.
+
+Tests: tests/006_CoordSeq.phpt with 31 sub-cases covering construct
+2D/3D/2DM/3DM, all setters/getters, throw paths for hasZ/hasM
+violations, copyFrom/To round-trips, getCoordSeq on each valid
+geometry type plus throw paths, clone semantics.
+
+Test suite: 7/7 green (existing 6 + new 6).
