+Subject: [PATCH 5/8] Items 6,12,16: GeoJSON I/O classes, curved geometry
+ constructors, factory statics
+MIME-Version: 1.0
+Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
+Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit
+
+22 new methods, 5 new module constants, 3 new .phpt files (36 sub-tests).
+
+Item 6 - GeoJSON I/O
+  GEOSGeoJSONReader::__construct, read($json)
+  GEOSGeoJSONWriter::__construct, write($g, $indent=-1),
+                    setOutputDimension($dim), getOutputDimension()
+  Note: Reader is permissive — accepts FeatureCollection and Feature
+  (returning GeometryCollection / inner geom respectively), not just
+  bare geometry. Behavior pinned in tests for forward compatibility.
+
+Item 12 - Curved geometry constructors (depends on CoordSeq)
+  GEOSGeometry::createCircularString, createEmptyCircularString
+  GEOSGeometry::createCompoundCurve, createEmptyCompoundCurve
+  GEOSGeometry::createCurvePolygon, createEmptyCurvePolygon
+  Constants: GEOS_CIRCULARSTRING=8, GEOS_COMPOUNDCURVE=9,
+             GEOS_CURVEPOLYGON=10, GEOS_MULTICURVE=11,
+             GEOS_MULTISURFACE=12
+  Curved geoms work for storage and WKT/WKB I/O. Overlay/buffer ops
+  still raise (libgeos limitation in 3.14).
+
+Item 16 - Geometry construction factories (depends on CoordSeq)
+  GEOSGeometry::createPoint, createPointFromXY, createEmptyPoint,
+  createLineString, createEmptyLineString, createLinearRing,
+  createPolygon, createEmptyPolygon,
+  createCollection, createEmptyCollection,
+  createRectangle
+
+CoordSeq + sub-geometry ownership transfers correctly into
+constructed geometries; consumed inputs' relays are NULL'd to
+prevent double-free. Reused-after-consumption raises a clean
+exception. All-or-nothing semantics for multi-input arrays:
+inputs are validated before any C handoff.
+
+18/18 .phpt tests pass.
