+From 7ddf5bebc7b996d5044bb9ed7b8d7d3d5ad9f44c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: Abraham van der Merwe <abz@frogfoot.com>
+Date: Sun, 26 Apr 2026 17:18:57 +0200
+Subject: [PATCH 7/8] Item 17: GEOSSTRtree spatial index
+MIME-Version: 1.0
+Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
+Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit
+
+New class GEOSSTRtree wrapping libgeos's STRtree:
+  __construct(int $nodeCapacity = 10)  — validates >= 2
+  insert(GEOSGeometry $env, mixed $payload)
+  remove(GEOSGeometry $env, mixed $payload) : bool
+  query(GEOSGeometry $env, ?callable $cb = null) : array
+  iterate(callable $cb) : void
+  nearest(GEOSGeometry $g) : mixed
+
+Implementation highlights:
+- Boxed-payload model (Q5.3 (a)): each insert allocates a small box
+  containing the payload zval + a cloned envelope. The C tree only
+  stores box pointers; PHP-side relay hash tracks live boxes for
+  cleanup-on-destroy. Dtor walks hash, frees boxes (dropping zval
+  refcounts), then destroys the GEOS tree.
+- Callback-thrown exceptions captured into a sticky-error flag
+  (Q5.8 (a)); subsequent callback invocations short-circuit; the
+  exception is rethrown at the PHP boundary after GEOS iteration
+  completes. Cannot abort GEOS callbacks mid-iteration.
+- 'remove' equality semantic: object identity for objects,
+  zend_is_identical (===) for scalars/arrays.
+- Build-once policy enforced: 'insert' after first 'query'/'iterate'
+  throws explicitly rather than silently dropping items.
+- 'nearest' uses GEOSSTRtree_nearest_generic_r with a custom
+  distance callback (the simpler '_nearest_r' assumes payloads are
+  GEOSGeometry* pointers — incompatible with our boxed-payload
+  scheme). Probe vs stored-item disambiguated by pointer identity
+  against the userdata.
+
+Tests: tests/030_STRtree.phpt with 18 sub-cases covering construct,
+collect-mode + callback-mode query, mixed-type payloads, iterate,
+nearest, remove, callback exception propagation, build-once
+rejection, refcount lifecycle (via WeakReference). Valgrind-clean.
+
+22/22 .phpt tests pass.
